{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba gate.py | sed -n '121,143p'; ls gate-run17*; sed -n '1,30p' round46u-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"   121\t# ---------- R2: old-2 call 8734 (v29 equity commitments) ----------\n   122\tR2_FAMILY = {'members': {'v29': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', CO, 'end of FY2027'),\n   123\t                                 'bands': [[None, 25], [25, 50], [50, 75], [75, 100], [100, None]]}},\n   124\t             'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n   125\tR2_PASSAGES = store_passages('old-2', ['e2620', 'e2889', 'e1732'])\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef r2():\n   129\t    eic = 'equity investment commitments'\n   130\t    return {'figures': [\n   131\t        src('bal', 'e2620', '$25 billion', 25.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'as of 2026-07-26')),\n   132\t        src('add18', 'e2889', '$18 billion', 18.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027')),\n   133\t        est('mtk', 3.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027'), 'the MediaTek investment announced after the balance date'),\n   134\t        est('talks', 6.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027'), 'the Anthropic and Thinking Machines talks, risk-adjusted (amount inferred from the stated $53B total)'),\n   135\t        src('ref70', 'e1732', '$70 billion', 70.0, 'USD bn', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'equity investments to ecosystem partners', CO, 'period not specified')),\n   136\t        comp('end', 'roll_forward', ['bal', 'add18', 'mtk', 'talks'], 53.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'end of FY2027'),\n   137\t             relation='overlap_unknown', disputed='add18'),\n   138\t    ], 'answers': [ans('v29', 'end', 3, {'figure': 'ref70'})]}                     # as stored: Bank of America's $70B\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t# ---------- R3: old-2 call 8595 (v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 data-center capex) ----------\n   142\tFOUR = 'four largest AI hyperscalers'\n   143\tR3_FAMILY = {'members': {'v6': {'what': W(FOUR, 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2027'),\ngate-run17.fixtures.json\ngate-run17.txt\n# Council round 46u: after 46t (read-only, same thread)\n\n46t answered:\n1. Boundary records carry certainty per boundary (definite and possible lists); bounds are carried through recomputation (_evaluate_bounded). R4b3 records definite [40] and possible [20, 30, 50]; R4one passes the bounded outcome through a one-input sum and still records definite [40].\n2. C3: when either side has a bound, the part exceeds its whole only when no pair of allowed values fits (part minimum above whole maximum); closed ranges and points keep the paired-end rule. R1qb (strictly above an exact whole) refused; R1qc (above 130 against at least 127.1) passes.\n\nGate run 17: 68 of 68. Mutants: 34 of 34 caught. render-r1 clean.\n\nAnswer GATE PASS STANDS or GATE FAIL, sorting any finding as (A) blocking or (B) a relabelling for the blind readers. Only (A) blocks. If no (A) remains, say GATE PASS STANDS.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport pathlib,json,io,contextlib,copy,types\nimport gate as g, calc_check as c, render_v13 as r, mutants\ndef replay(func, log):\n    p=io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(p): status=func()\n    assert status==0 and p.getvalue()==pathlib.Path(log).read_text()\nreplay(g.main,'\\\\''gate-run17.txt'\\\\'')\nassert g.MANIFEST==json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''gate-run17.fixtures.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nreplay(r.main,'\\\\''render-r1.txt'\\\\'')\noriginal=g.cc\npath=pathlib.Path('\\\\''calc_check.py'\\\\'')\nsrc=path.read_text()\nfor name,old,new,target in mutants.MUTANTS:\n    g.cc=original\n    if old:\n        assert src.count(old)==1,name\n        mod=types.ModuleType('\\\\''in_memory_calc_check'\\\\'')\n        exec(compile(src.replace(old,new),str(path),'\\\\''exec'\\\\''),mod.__dict__)\n        g.cc=mod\n    misses={name for name,ok,_,_ in g.run() if not ok}\n    assert (target in misses if target else not misses),(name,misses)\ng.cc=original\nprint('\\\\''68 gate items, 34 mutants and stored render reproduced'\\\\'')\ndef fig(calc,fid):\n    return next(f for f in calc['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']==fid)\ndef check(name,case,passages):\n    fam,x=case['\\\\''family'\\\\''],case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\n    schema=r.v13_schema(list(fam['\\\\''members'\\\\'']),list(passages),[])\n    wire=r.strict(x,schema)\n    clean=r.without_nulls(wire)\n    report=c.check(fam,passages,clean)\n    print(name,r.model.check_schema(wire,schema),report,c.publish_decision(fam,clean,report))\nfor name,ps in (('\\\\''R4b3'\\\\'',g.R4_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R4one'\\\\'',g.R4_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R1qb'\\\\'',g.R1_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R1qc'\\\\'',g.R1_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R2'\\\\'',g.R2_PASSAGES)):\n    check(name,g.MANIFEST[name],ps)\ncase=copy.deepcopy(g.MANIFEST['\\\\''R2'\\\\''])\nx=case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\nfig(x,'\\\\''talks'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'',basis_text='\\\\''A lower bound on estimated additional commitments'\\\\'')\nfig(x,'\\\\''end'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'')\ncheck('\\\\''R2 retains non-disputed input >6.5'\\\\'',case,g.R2_PASSAGES)\ncase=copy.deepcopy(g.MANIFEST['\\\\''R2'\\\\''])\nx=case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\nfig(x,'\\\\''talks'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'',basis_text='\\\\''An estimated lower bound on withdrawals from commitments'\\\\'')\nfig(x,'\\\\''end'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'',value=40.0,signs=[1,1,1,-1])\ncheck('\\\\''R2 signed flow reverses bound: wrong >40 on rung 3'\\\\'',case,g.R2_PASSAGES)\nfig(x,'\\\\''end'\\\\'')['\\\\''bound'\\\\'']='\\\\''<'\\\\''\nx['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]['\\\\''rung'\\\\'']=2\ncheck('\\\\''R2 signed flow reverses bound: correct <40 on rung 2'\\\\'',case,g.R2_PASSAGES)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport pathlib,json,io,contextlib,copy,types\nimport gate as g, calc_check as c, render_v13 as r, mutants\ndef replay(func, log):\n    p=io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(p): status=func()\n    assert status==0 and p.getvalue()==pathlib.Path(log).read_text()\nreplay(g.main,'\\\\''gate-run17.txt'\\\\'')\nassert g.MANIFEST==json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''gate-run17.fixtures.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nreplay(r.main,'\\\\''render-r1.txt'\\\\'')\noriginal=g.cc\npath=pathlib.Path('\\\\''calc_check.py'\\\\'')\nsrc=path.read_text()\nfor name,old,new,target in mutants.MUTANTS:\n    g.cc=original\n    if old:\n        assert src.count(old)==1,name\n        mod=types.ModuleType('\\\\''in_memory_calc_check'\\\\'')\n        exec(compile(src.replace(old,new),str(path),'\\\\''exec'\\\\''),mod.__dict__)\n        g.cc=mod\n    misses={name for name,ok,_,_ in g.run() if not ok}\n    assert (target in misses if target else not misses),(name,misses)\ng.cc=original\nprint('\\\\''68 gate items, 34 mutants and stored render reproduced'\\\\'')\ndef fig(calc,fid):\n    return next(f for f in calc['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']==fid)\ndef check(name,case,passages):\n    fam,x=case['\\\\''family'\\\\''],case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\n    schema=r.v13_schema(list(fam['\\\\''members'\\\\'']),list(passages),[])\n    wire=r.strict(x,schema)\n    clean=r.without_nulls(wire)\n    report=c.check(fam,passages,clean)\n    print(name,r.model.check_schema(wire,schema),report,c.publish_decision(fam,clean,report))\nfor name,ps in (('\\\\''R4b3'\\\\'',g.R4_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R4one'\\\\'',g.R4_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R1qb'\\\\'',g.R1_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R1qc'\\\\'',g.R1_PASSAGES),('\\\\''R2'\\\\'',g.R2_PASSAGES)):\n    check(name,g.MANIFEST[name],ps)\ncase=copy.deepcopy(g.MANIFEST['\\\\''R2'\\\\''])\nx=case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\nfig(x,'\\\\''talks'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'',basis_text='\\\\''A lower bound on estimated additional commitments'\\\\'')\nfig(x,'\\\\''end'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'')\ncheck('\\\\''R2 retains non-disputed input >6.5'\\\\'',case,g.R2_PASSAGES)\ncase=copy.deepcopy(g.MANIFEST['\\\\''R2'\\\\''])\nx=case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\nfig(x,'\\\\''talks'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'',basis_text='\\\\''An estimated lower bound on withdrawals from commitments'\\\\'')\nfig(x,'\\\\''end'\\\\'').update(bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'',value=40.0,signs=[1,1,1,-1])\ncheck('\\\\''R2 signed flow reverses bound: wrong >40 on rung 3'\\\\'',case,g.R2_PASSAGES)\nfig(x,'\\\\''end'\\\\'')['\\\\''bound'\\\\'']='\\\\''<'\\\\''\nx['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]['\\\\''rung'\\\\'']=2\ncheck('\\\\''R2 signed flow reverses bound: correct <40 on rung 2'\\\\'',case,g.R2_PASSAGES)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"68 gate items, 34 mutants and stored render reproduced\nR4b3 [] {'errors': [], 'recorded': [{'type': 'adjustment', 'figure': 'vera28', 'outcome': 'v41', 'value': [None, 40.0], 'alternate': [40.0, None], 'alternate_bound': '>', 'definite': [40], 'possible': [20, 30, 50]}]} publish\nR4one [] {'errors': [], 'recorded': [{'type': 'adjustment', 'figure': 'vera28', 'outcome': 'v41', 'value': [None, 40.0], 'alternate': [40.0, None], 'alternate_bound': '>', 'definite': [40], 'possible': [20, 30, 50]}]} publish\nR1qb [] {'errors': [('C3', 'FY2027 Q4 base: v9 dcq4 (127.1, False, inf, False) exceeds v14 q4f (127.1, True, 127.1, True)')], 'recorded': [{'type': 'bridge', 'figure': 'q4f', 'bridge': 'carry', 'alternate': 'undetermined'}]} refused\nR1qc [] {'errors': [], 'recorded': []} publish\nR2 [] {'errors': [], 'recorded': [{'type': 'overlap', 'figure': 'end', 'outcome': 'v29', 'value': [53.0, 53.0], 'alternate': [35.0, 35.0], 'alternate_bound': None, 'definite': [50], 'possible': []}]} publish\nR2 retains non-disputed input >6.5 [] {'errors': [], 'recorded': [{'type': 'overlap', 'figure': 'end', 'outcome': 'v29', 'value': [53.0, None], 'alternate': [35.0, 35.0], 'alternate_bound': None, 'definite': [50], 'possible': [75, 100]}]} publish\nR2 signed flow reverses bound: wrong >40 on rung 3 [] {'errors': [], 'recorded': [{'type': 'overlap', 'figure': 'end', 'outcome': 'v29', 'value': [40.0, None], 'alternate': [22.0, 22.0], 'alternate_bound': None, 'definite': [25], 'possible': [50, 75, 100]}]} publish\nR2 signed flow reverses bound: correct <40 on rung 2 [] {'errors': [('C2', 'end: its inputs make it a lower bound, but it is declared <')], 'recorded': [{'type': 'overlap', 'figure': 'end', 'outcome': 'v29', 'value': [40.0, None], 'alternate': [22.0, 22.0], 'alternate_bound': None, 'definite': [25], 'possible': [50, 75, 100]}]} refused\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"GATE FAIL\n\n**A — Blocking.** The registered cases pass, but two R2 replays show that recomputation still loses bounds.\n\n- **Removing the disputed addition turns a lower bound into a point.** With a retained input of `>$6.5B`, removing the disputed $18B changes the total from `>$53B` to `>$35B`. The checker records exactly $35B and calls the $50B crossing definite. The alternate could still exceed $50B. [Overlap recomputation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:773)\n- **Subtracting a bounded outflow keeps the wrong bound direction.** Subtracting `>$6.5B` from $46.5B gives `<$40B`. The checker refused that result and accepted `>$40B` on the $50–75B rung because bound propagation ignores the minus sign. [Bound propagation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:150)\n\nUse the same bound-aware arithmetic for the original calculation and its alternate, including each retained operand’s sign. Add both R2 cases to the gate.\n\n**B — Non-blocking.** No relabelling findings."}}
